course: dictionary
lesson: 7555
title: Prehistoric: before written history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Break the word into parts. Pre- means before, as in preview. History is the story of the past that people wrote down. So prehistoric means before written history began, a time when nobody had written anything down yet.
explain: «We learn about prehistoric people from cave paintings, bones and tools, not from books.» Books did not exist yet, so the clues are the paintings, bones and tools. You can use the same clue-hunting skill for any word.
explain: Prehistoric can also be a joke. «My grandad's old mobile phone is prehistoric, it only makes calls.» Here it does not mean from long ago. It means very old-fashioned and out of date.
fact: Prehistoric means from the very long time before people wrote things down.
fact: Prehistoric times include the Stone Age, the Bronze Age and the Iron Age.
fact: Prehistoric animals include dinosaurs and woolly mammoths.
fact: We learn about prehistoric people from cave paintings, bones and tools.
fact: Informally, prehistoric can joke that something is very old-fashioned, like an old phone or computer.
exercise: «We learn about prehistoric people from cave paintings, bones and tools.» What does prehistoric mean? | From the year 2000 | Wild and dangerous | Made of stone and very strong | *From before people wrote things down
exercise: Which of these animals lived in prehistoric times? | Printed newspaper | Bicycle | *Woolly mammoth | Smartphone
exercise: In the word preview, the part pre- means the same as in prehistoric. What does pre- mean? | *Before | Not | Under | Again
test: Jo says her old games console is prehistoric. What does she mean as a joke? | Made of stone | Very new and shiny | From the Stone Age | *Very old-fashioned and out of date
test: Which of these is a prehistoric time? | Victorian times | The year 2050 | *Stone Age | Tudor times
exam: Which sentence uses prehistoric as a joke about something old-fashioned? | «The bones were found in a prehistoric cave.» | «The cave paintings are prehistoric.» | «Our class studied prehistoric animals.» | *«My grandad's mobile phone is prehistoric, it only makes calls.»
